{"time": "2026-06-08T22:38:31", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "a_language_drift_g002_a01_7960cd0e_001", "post_id": "sgh4qda", "subreddit": "GlobalTalk", "content": "We keep talking about \"billion-dollar aid packages\" for Ukraine like we're just writing a giant check, but it really comes down to actual factory shifts. If the assembly lines aren't running round-the-clock to stamp out physical artillery shells, the money means nothing. It's a basic manufacturing bottleneck, not just a political debate."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:38:31", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "a_language_drift_g002_a01_7960cd0e_007", "post_id": "krs6mxa", "subreddit": "news", "content": "Tired of the PR about European shell deliveries to Ukraine. The actual factory output numbers from BAE and Rheinmetall show we won't see real volume until late 2024. You can't defend a trench with press releases."}
